# Interactive-ready controls

**Activation:** when adding or changing SPA views, loading states, overlays, or thin-hook fetch shapes.

## Law

> If a control is not ready, do not show it. If it is shown, it must be immediately interactive.

## Definitions

- **Control** — link, button, combobox, tab, sort header, pagination link, or form field with submit.
- **Ready** — backing data/state exists for the control's action; no in-flight fetch blocks the action.
- **Shown** — visible in the layout (not `hidden`, not zero-size, not inside a collapsed panel the user has not opened).

## Required patterns

1. **First paint, zero data** — full-page `LoadingMessage` / skeleton with **no** interactive chrome (Search, TypeDetail pattern).
2. **Refetch with prior data** — `keepPreviousData` + `tableBusy` / `sectionBusy`: dim + `aria-busy`, **never** `pointer-events-none` on containers holding links ([`JobList.tsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/views/JobList.tsx) test contract).
3. **Secondary sections** — hide, collapse, or skeleton until ready where appropriate; JobList **filter options** may defer until first paint, but **distributions** default open and fetch on JobList mount (optional Collapsible collapse after).
4. **User-initiated in-flight action** — `disabled` on the **same** button the user clicked (`rotating` on PageApiKey) is allowed.
5. **Bokeh** — defer embed until section visible (`deferEmbedUntilVisible` default); no Unavailable while `isLoading` ([`design-focused-spa-ux.mdc`](design-focused-spa-ux.mdc), [`job-plot-artifacts-caching.mdc`](job-plot-artifacts-caching.mdc)).
6. **Bokeh list/dashboard preview** — Job-list (and same-pattern) thumbnail/grid embeds must use **`previewMode`** on [`BokehEmbed`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/components/BokehEmbed.tsx): `pointer-events-none` on the **plot root only** (`.bokeh-embed`), skip global `scheduleBokehLayoutReflow` / continuous maximize-on-`resize`. Enlarge / full interactive embeds must **not** set `previewMode`.

## Forbidden patterns

- `pointer-events-none` on a parent wrapping sort links, table rows, or pagination (except `aria-hidden` decorative spans). **Allowed/required** on preview plot canvases when `previewMode` is set (not on Enlarge controls or table chrome).
- In-page sticky headers/tabs above **`--z-sticky-inpage`** (10) except portaled modal/floating UI — never reuse modal-tier z-index (e.g. `z-1010`) on table headers.
- Visible combobox/select/button rendered `disabled` while options or section data load — use skeleton rows or omit the control ([`JobListHeaderFilters.tsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/components/JobListHeaderFilters.tsx)).
- Full-page skeleton replacing an already-rendered interactive surface on refetch.
- Mounting Bokeh into `hidden` or zero-size subtrees.
- Modal backdrop blocking unrelated page chrome when `modal={false}` — omit overlay ([`dialog.tsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/components/ui/dialog.tsx) `showOverlay={false}`).
- Focus trap stealing Tab when focus is outside the trapped panel ([`useFocusTrap.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/hooks/useFocusTrap.ts)).
- Nested `max-h-* overflow-auto` **list scrollers** for **paginated** tables when document scroll is available — one page scrollbar only ([`JobList.tsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/views/JobList.tsx)).
- Absolute-positioned `<tr>` virtualization inside a semantic `<table>` (breaks header/body column alignment).
- Synchronous Bokeh `prepareBokehJsonItemForEmbed` / `embed_item` for large payloads without yielding to the main thread first ([`yield-main-thread.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/utils/yield-main-thread.ts)).
- List/dashboard histogram thumbs that omit `previewMode` (live interactive canvas + global resize reflow after ready).

## Nested portaled overlays (outside-dismiss)

Any custom outside-dismiss (dialog, drawer, collapse — including Extended Search in [`Layout.tsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/Layout.tsx)) must treat portaled overlay roots as **inside** the open surface:

- `data-slot="select-content"`
- `data-slot="popover-content"`
- `data-slot="dropdown-menu-content"`
- `data-slot="dropdown-menu-sub-content"`

Use [`isPortaledOverlayTarget`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/utils/is-portaled-overlay-target.ts) (or an equivalent `closest` check). Do **not** rely solely on a panel `ref.contains(target)` — Select/Popover/Dropdown portals mount under `document.body`.

**Regression required:** open the parent surface, open a nested Select/Popover, activate an option or click overlay content, and assert the parent stays open. Keep a separate case that a genuine outside click still closes the parent.

## URL scoped updates (site-wide)

Query-string / path changes must **not** remount or blank surfaces whose **identity** did not change. Separate keys:

| Kind | Examples | Effect |
|------|----------|--------|
| **Identity / filter** | `end_time__date`, `username`, `queue`, host/`pk`/`jid` path segments | May refetch primary **and** filter-dependent secondary data |
| **Presentation** | `order_by`, `page`, `view`/`tab` (local chrome) | Refetch **primary** with `keepPreviousData` / `*Busy`; must **not** clear secondary panels, enlarge dialogs, or filter popovers |

**Presentation chrome vs placeholder payload:** under `keepPreviousData`, table **rows** and server-only fields like `num_pages` may lag. Pagination **active page** (`aria-current` / `isActive`) and sort indicators must still read **`page` / `order_by` from the URL** — not from the stale response — so sort→paginate does not freeze on the previous page. Reference: [`JobList.tsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/views/JobList.tsx); regression in `JobList.test.tsx` (URL page active while mock response still reports old `pagination.page` / `order_by`).

### Required

1. Secondary fetches (JobList histograms, HostDetail plot params) use a **filter-identity** param set — strip presentation keys before the request key.
2. Do **not** `setX(null)` on secondary state when only presentation keys change; use an updating flag (`histogramsUpdating`, `*Busy`) until new identity data arrives.
3. Enlarge / filter combobox open state resets on **filter-identity** key only (not full `searchParams.toString()`). Layout nav chrome may still reset on full QS.
4. If a hook exposes `tableBusy` / `detailBusy` / `sectionBusy` / `refetchBusy`, the view **must** use it — never full-page `LoadingMessage` on refetch when prior data exists.
5. First paint with zero data may still use full-page `LoadingMessage` / skeleton.
6. Clear job plots only when **`pk`** changes — not when a tab `enabled` flag toggles.
7. **Soft presentation navigation** — JobList sort / pagination / `view` tab must use `router.replace` with `{ scroll: false }` (via [`soft-presentation-nav.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/utils/soft-presentation-nav.ts) / [`replace-path-if-changed.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/utils/replace-path-if-changed.ts)), not bare Next `<Link>` / `PaginationLink` default navigation that remounts the lazy view.
8. **JobDetail analysis tabs** — keep tab in React `useState`; sync `?tab=` with [`replace-tab-history.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/utils/replace-tab-history.ts) (`history.replaceState`). Do **not** use `router.replace` for tab chrome (it remounts the lazy `JobDetail` under App Router).
9. **Suspense flash** — after the first machine lazy view resolves, `machine-route-client` Suspense fallback must be `null` (not `"Loading page…"`) so query-only presentation nav does not blank the page.

Helpers: [`filter-identity-params.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/utils/filter-identity-params.ts), [`build-job-list-api-params.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/utils/build-job-list-api-params.ts) (`buildJobListHistogramApiParams`), [`soft-presentation-nav.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/utils/soft-presentation-nav.ts), [`replace-tab-history.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/utils/replace-tab-history.ts).

## Thin-hook loading shapes

| Flag | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `initialLoading` | `isLoading && !data` — first payload only; may gate full-page skeleton |
| `tableBusy` / `detailBusy` / `sectionBusy` | `isFetching && !isLoading` with stale data visible — dim only, keep interactive |
| `optionsLoading` / `sectionInitialLoading` | Scoped to one panel; must not gate entire page |

Reference hooks: [`use-job-list.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/hooks/use-job-list.ts), [`use-job-detail.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/hooks/use-job-detail.ts), [`use-admin-monitor-section.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/hooks/use-admin-monitor-section.ts).

## Reference implementations

- **JobList** — table first; deferred `filter_options`; distributions default open / always fetch; histogram params omit `order_by`/`page`; **document-scroll** table rows (no nested max-h virtualizer); histogram thumbs/mobile grid use **`previewMode`**; Enlarge stays interactive; soft sort/pagination (`scroll: false`); pagination/`order_by` chrome from **URL** while rows may lag on `keepPreviousData`; `JobList.test.tsx` (`tableBusy` not pointer-blocked; stale-placeholder page active).
- **JobDetail** — `initialLoading` only on first paint; tabs stay mounted during `detailsLoading`; tab chrome via `useState` + `history.replaceState`; plots clear on `pk` only; deep-link test in `JobDetail.test.tsx`.
- **HostDetail / TypeDetail** — `keepPreviousData` + `detailBusy` (no full-page blank on refetch).
- **JobMonitor / AdminMonitor / ClusterDashboard** — progressive `*Busy`; paginated tables use document scroll (no nested list scrollers).

## Tests

- Extend Vitest when changing loading UX: assert shown controls lack blocking `pointer-events-none` on parent containers.
- Run drift guard: `src/utils/interactive-ready-drift.test.ts` (scoped-render contracts for hist params, Host/Type busy, plots-on-pk, AdminMonitor keepPrevious; **no nested max-h + useVirtualizer** in JobList/JobMonitor/AdminMonitor).
- Nested overlay dismiss: [`Layout.test.tsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/Layout.test.tsx) — open Extended Search, choose a portaled Select option / click help popover; parent stays open; genuine outside click still closes.

